    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Nestled in a quiet cul-de-sac within the mature and highly sought-after Castletown development, No. 31 The Woodlands is a charming three-bedroom semi-detached bungalow offering an exceptional opportunity to acquire a well-located home in one of Celbridge's most desirable residential settings.\r\n\r\nThis attractive property extends to a spacious and well-balanced layout, with bright and comfortable accommodation throughout. The accommodation comprises an inviting entrance hallway, a generous living room, a kitchen/dining area, three well-proportioned bedrooms, and a family bathroom. \r\n\r\nExternally, the property benefits from a private rear garden, providing an ideal space for outdoor dining, gardening, or relaxation. To the front, there is a garden and off-street parking. Its enviable position within a peaceful cul-de-sac ensures a safe and tranquil environment while maintaining close proximity to all local amenities.\r\n\r\nThe Woodlands enjoys an unrivalled location adjacent to the historic Castletown Estate and within walking distance of Celbridge village, where a wide range of shops, cafés, restaurants, schools, and recreational facilities can be found. Excellent transport links, including the M4 motorway and Hazelhatch railway station, provide easy access to Dublin City Centre and beyond.\r\n\r\nCombining the convenience of single-storey living with a prime residential location, No. 31 presents an outstanding opportunity for downsizers, first-time buyers, investors, or those seeking a home with future potential in the heart of Celbridge.\r\n\r\n\r\nFeatures:\r\n• Three-bedroom semi-detached bungalow\r\n• Quiet cul-de-sac location\r\n• Mature and established residential development\r\n• Bright, well-proportioned accommodation\r\n• Private rear garden\r\n• Off-street parking\r\n• Excellent potential to modernise and extend (subject to planning permission)\r\n• Walking distance to Celbridge village and local amenities\r\n• Adjacent to Castletown Estate and parklands\r\n• Easy access to M4 motorway and Hazelhatch railway station"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance Porch:\t\r\n\r\nReception Hall: with laminate wood floor and hotpress \r\n\t\r\nLounge:  feature open fireplace with marble hearth and wooden mantle, laminate wood floor and TV point \t\t\r\n6.9x3.5m\t\r\n\r\nKitchen/Dining Room:  with range of wall and floor mounted fitted kitchen units, laminate wood floor, breakfast bar, electric cooker, plumbed for washing machine patio doors to rear garden\r\n5.5x2.9m\t\r\n\r\nBedroom 1: with built in wardrobes, laminate wood floor and TV point \r\n3.3x3.4m\r\n\r\nBedroom 2: with built in wardrobes and laminate wood floor\r\n2.6x3.5m\r\n\r\nBedroom 3:  with built in wardrobes and laminate wood floor\r\n2.4x2.1m\r\n\r\nBathroom: with Triton electric shower, W.C and W.H.B, fully tiled walls and tiled floor"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Outside\r\nFront garden with driveway, laid out in lawn with hedged boundary  \r\nRear garden laid out in lawn with walled and fenced boundary and mature trees \r\nPaved patio area \r\nTimber garden shed \r\n\r\nServices\r\nGFCH\r\nPVC glazed windows \r\n\r\n\r\nLocal Area Information\r\nPublic transport routes that service Castletown:\r\nBus: C4/C6/W6\r\nNearby Areas: Castletown House, Celbridge & Maynooth"
      },
